P18-V01 ChannelHandle identity slice (2026-10-16)

- Compared pinned Java client source at `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`:
  `ResponseFuture.getChannel()` returns its stored channel, and every
  `ChannelEventListener` callback receives a `Channel` object.
- Rust already exposes the corresponding capability through `ResponseFuture::channel()`
  and callback/event `ChannelHandle`s. Added identity assertions proving that
  `ResponseFuture::channel()` retains the supplied handle and that CONNECT and
  ACTIVE events/callbacks for one connection share the same handle identity.
- Validation: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --all-features --locked`
  passed (102 unit, 8 codec, 1 fuzz regression, 7 security, 101 transport,
  and 8 doctests); `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` passed.
- Strict Remoting Clippy first found a test `MutexGuard` held across shutdown
  await; the guard was scoped before the await. The rerun
  `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --all-targets --all-features
  --locked -- -D warnings` passed.
- The Java reference checkout remained read-only. No plan file was changed.
